# Sieve's Algorithm

# Definition
'''
The Sieve of Eratosthenes is an algorithm used to find all prime numbers from 2 up to a given number (N) in an efficient way.
Instead of checking each number one by one to see if it is prime, the algorithm removes (marks) all multiples of prime numbers. 
After removing all composite numbers, the numbers that remain are the prime numbers.
'''

# Main Idea
'''
The algorithm starts with the smallest prime number, 2.
Mark all multiples of 2 as not prime.
Move to the next number that is still not marked (which will be 3).
Mark all multiples of 3 as not prime.
Continue the same process for the remaining prime numbers.
At the end, the numbers that are not marked are the prime numbers.
'''
